      "writtenOn": "2020-03-10T23:52:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this get the ordering right so it is called after cbi_init()?",
      "revId": "d02975b99331831fbf191ede0dc896d57c2aff22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "74448f9c_46c5ba76",
        "filename": "board/morphius/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 246,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-11T18:27:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "cbi_init is called at DECLARE_HOOK(HOOK_INIT, cbi_init, HOOK_PRIO_INIT_I2C + 1);\nThis is the same hook type, but the priority on cbi_init is 3 versus 5000 for setup_mux.\n\nIf I am reading this correctly, I believe this is fine\n\nI set my FW_CONFIG in cbi and this definitely came up after cbi_init was called.",
      "parentUuid": "7bcb0257_d5ddd0b2",
      "revId": "d02975b99331831fbf191ede0dc896d57c2aff22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ac688ff1_633759fb",
        "filename": "board/morphius/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 246,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-11T18:38:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yep, that should be fine for setup_mux.\nThere is some danger that something else in the future (eg sensor init) might happen before cbi_init(), which will lead to trouble. How hard is it to add an error message if someone reads fw_config before it has been set, so we can catch this if it happens?",
      "parentUuid": "74448f9c_46c5ba76",
      "revId": "d02975b99331831fbf191ede0dc896d57c2aff22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "8d612b6a_99883b99",
        "filename": "board/morphius/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 246,
      "author": {
        "id": 1346479
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-11T19:52:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe CBI requires I2C.  That would be the reason for th HOOK_PRIO_INIT_I2C+1.  I would guess most sensors are going to require I2C as well.  cbi_init is not required to run before fw_config gets used.  This is just the first time it is typically called but if someone else calls to get the fw_config information, after I2C is initialized, the call will work fine and that will be the call that is cached instead of the one from cbi_init.  I don\u0027t think there is an issue in this path",
      "parentUuid": "ac688ff1_633759fb",
      "revId": "d02975b99331831fbf191ede0dc896d57c2aff22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "d61dd07e_b08704aa",
        "filename": "board/morphius/board.c",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 246,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-03-11T20:02:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Oh right, cbi_init() isn\u0027t doing the caching now.\nI guess we will already print an error if get_cbi_fw_config() fails (eg if I2C isn\u0027t initialized yet), so that should cover it.",
      "parentUuid": "8d612b6a_99883b99",
      "revId": "d02975b99331831fbf191ede0dc896d57c2aff22",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
